<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siddis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Siddhi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siddis are a community of African descent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>. On the western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Siddi rulers of Janjira maintained a naval power. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> note that Maratha fleets challenged Siddi and Portuguese maritime forces along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siddis.jpg" alt="Siddis" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagarjun Kandukuru from Bangalore, India · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siddi_community_(16527139018).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The court and army drew on three main groups: Persian, Turkish and Arab immigrants known as Westerners (gharibs), Deccani Muslims long settled in the region, and Africans, called <b>Habshis</b>, many of whom had arrived as slaves and rose to high command.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bijapur-sultanate">Bijapur Sultanate · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Marathas also built an effective navy, with sea forts such as Sindhudurg and Vijaydurg, to defend the Konkan coast against the Portuguese and the <b>Siddis</b> of Janjira; under Kanhoji Angre in the early 18th century it challenged even the English and Dutch.</blockquote><a href="/empire/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>It later passed to the <b>Siddis</b> of Janjira, the African-descended naval chiefs of the Konkan coast, who kept it as a distant dependency.</blockquote><a href="/state/jafrabad-state">Jafrabad State</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Siddis</b>, Muslims of East African (Habshi) origin, held the island fort of Janjira off Murud as officers of the Ahmadnagar Sultanate; tradition dates their control to 1489.</blockquote><a href="/state/janjira-state">Janjira State</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Siddis</b>, of East African descent, ruled the island fortress of Janjira on the Konkan coast.</blockquote><a href="/state/sachin-state">Sachin State</a></li></ul></section>
